(O112 - Calibrate Bare Spindle Nose)
(Step 2 of tool setter setup:)
(Probes the bare spindle nose (no tool) at the tool setter)
(to establish the zero reference for all tool measurements.)
(This is the "master" reference that all tools are compared against.)
(Call as: O112 call)
(Requires: [TOOL_SETTER] X, Y, VEL in INI)
(Requires: [PROBE] Z_SAFE in INI)

O112 sub

    #<setter_x> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]X>
    #<setter_y> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]Y>
    #<setter_vel> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]VEL>
    #<max_depth> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]MAX_PROBE_DEPTH>
    #<z_safe> = #<_ini[PROBE]Z_SAFE>

    M5
    M9
    G90
    G40
    G49

    (Move to tool setter)
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>
    G53 G0 X#<setter_x> Y#<setter_y>

    (Probe the bare spindle nose)
    G91
    G38.2 Z[0 - #<max_depth>] F[#<setter_vel> * 4]
    G0 Z2.0
    G38.2 Z-4.0 F#<setter_vel>

    (The probed Z is the spindle nose position)
    #<spindle_nose_z> = #5063

    (This becomes the absolute reference. All tool lengths)
    (are measured as offsets from this position.)
    (Store in the tool table as tool 0 reference)

    (MSG, ========================================)
    (MSG, Bare Spindle Nose Calibration Complete)
    (MSG, Spindle nose probed at Z: #<spindle_nose_z>)
    (MSG, )
    (MSG, This is your absolute Z reference.)
    (MSG, All tool lengths will be measured relative)
    (MSG, to this position.)
    (MSG, ========================================)

    (Retract)
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>

O112 endsub
M2
